libblemesh example: provision and configure a mesh node
=======================================================

mesh_provision_configure.c is a worked, radio-free example of the libblemesh
network-manager (Configuration Client) API used by meshd(8) and meshctl(8).

It demonstrates, in one process:

  1. Creating a mesh network (primary NetKey/AppKey, IV Index) with this node
     as the Provisioner.
  2. Allocating a unicast address block and recording a provisioned node with
     its device key (DevKey) in the roster.
  3. Building the Configuration messages that commission the node -- Config
     AppKey Add and Config Model App Bind -- sealing each under the node's
     DevKey (AKF=0), and recovering them to prove the round-trip.
  4. Persisting the manager database (network keys, unicast allocator, roster
     and DevKeys) and reloading it.

This mirrors the meshctl(8) operator workflow:

    meshctl create-network
    meshctl provision <uuid> 1
    meshctl cfg appkey-add <addr>
    meshctl cfg model-bind <addr> <elem> <model>

Building
--------

The mesh_*.h headers are not installed system-wide yet, so build inside the
FreeBSD source tree:

    cd share/examples/libblemesh
    make
    ./mesh_provision_configure

See meshd(8) and meshctl(8) for the daemon and its command-line client.
